From a4c5df63314d756275a33fc02407b9cbe76194dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joakim Hansson <joakim.hansson87@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 22:02:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/36] vulkan: fused REPEAT+MUL+ADD kernel for broadcast
 scatter chains

New mul_bcast_add.comp computes dst = r + repeat(a) * repeat(w) in one
dispatch, replacing the REPEAT + broadcast MUL + ADD chain that the
qwen4exp hyper-connection combine runs twice per layer. The matcher
tolerates interleaved view nodes in the span; sources are declared
elementwise so the common in-place case (output reusing the residual's
buffer) stays fused - the shader reads r[idx] before writing d[idx].

Dispatches per decode token: 3119 -> 2929. Decode 26.9 -> 27.2 t/s
shallow, 23.9 -> 24.2 at 8k; prefill 345 -> 354 at 8k (Strix Halo,
RADV). Greedy output verified identical with fusion disabled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AUwCGmqs39JdaEFjBmtvDa
